# Visual draw distance. MAIN-THREAD cost, which is the part that matters.
#
# The GPU keys in 04-high could be priced individually because the stat line
# attributes GPU ms per pass. There is no equivalent for the main thread: it
# reports `main ms cache / far / snapshot` and nothing per feature. So these
# cannot be read off one run the way the GPU table can, and they need a real
# before/after. That is why this is a separate preset from 06-interactivity
# rather than one big push -- two bundles, two measured steps.
#
# Budget: the play profile caps at 158 fps on a 50-165 Hz G-Sync panel, which is
# 6.33 ms per frame against a measured 4.93 ms median. So 1.40 ms is spendable.
# That is not much for seven keys, and this bundle may well not fit. Not fitting
# is a result: bisect from here rather than creeping up from the floor, because
# cost is only attributable to a setting that is actually costing something.
#
# Measure with the cap OFF (python pzconfig.py --bench), or the frame time is
# pinned at 6.33 ms and the comparison tests nothing -- pzbench will say CAPPED
# RUN and refuse. Then come back to --play.
#
# interiorFurniture is the one with no distance to tune: it is furniture inside
# buildings you are not in, off entirely at present. The largest visual change
# here and the most likely to be expensive, since it adds geometry rather than
# extending a radius.
#
# UNMEASURED. Every number below is a judgement about what "further" should mean,
# not a value read from anywhere. The live values are in the comments.
target: viewpoint

pack.trueweathers.farShadows=true
lod.interiorFurniture=true
lod.farBlocks=26
lod.shellFullBlocks=4
lod.boxesFineBlocks=5
lod.treesFadeBlocks=12
lod.treesGoneBlocks=24
lod.farColoursFullBlocks=22
